  "description": "This chocolate-coated caramel honeycomb with peanuts is salty-sweet and satisfyingly crunchy. Plus: It takes less than 30 minutes to make.",
  "notes": "Notes: Once you start whisking the baking soda into the caramel, it will bubble up like crazy, so make sure the pan you're using is large enough (at least 2 1/2 quarts); otherwise the hot caramel could spill over the side of the saucepan. Also, please be careful when working with hot caramel and honeycomb. This stuff is hot!\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Honeycomb can be stored in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 5 days.",
